examples.question_text:
Find $x$ and give a reason.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.3,0)--(2.3,0);
\draw (0,0)--(65:2.3);
\draw (0,0)--(125:2.3);
\draw (0.65,0) arc (0:65:0.65);
\draw (65:0.85) arc (65:125:0.85);
\draw (125:0.65) arc (125:180:0.65);
\node at (32.5:1.25) {$x$};
\node at (95:1.35) {$60^{\circ}$};
\node at (152.5:1.25) {$55^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A right angle is split into three angles. Find $x$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,2.5)--(0,0)--(2.5,0);
\draw (0,0)--(24:2.5);
\draw (0,0)--(60:2.5);
\draw (0.23,0)--(0.23,0.23)--(0,0.23);
\draw (0.8,0) arc (0:24:0.8);
\draw (24:1.0) arc (24:60:1.0);
\draw (60:0.8) arc (60:90:0.8);
\node at (12:1.65) {$24^{\circ}$};
\node at (42:1.65) {$36^{\circ}$};
\node at (75:1.45) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the reflex angle $x$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \a in {0,65,150}{\draw (0,0)--(\a:2.3);}
\draw (0.7,0) arc (0:65:0.7);
\draw (65:0.9) arc (65:150:0.9);
\draw (150:0.7) arc (150:360:0.7);
\node at (32.5:1.3) {$65^{\circ}$};
\node at (107.5:1.45) {$85^{\circ}$};
\node at (255:1.15) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two straight lines intersect. Find $x$ and give a reason.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (28:2.3)--(208:2.3);
\draw (152:2.3)--(332:2.3);
\draw (28:0.7) arc (28:152:0.7);
\draw (208:0.7) arc (208:332:0.7);
\node at (90:1.2) {$124^{\circ}$};
\node at (270:1.2) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The angles around a point are $b^{\circ}$, $(2b)^{\circ}$, $(3b)^{\circ}$ and $210^{\circ}$. Determine $b$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \a in {0,25,75,150}{\draw (0,0)--(\a:2.6);}
\draw (1.0,0) arc (0:25:1.0);
\draw (25:0.85) arc (25:75:0.85);
\draw (75:0.7) arc (75:150:0.7);
\draw (150:0.85) arc (150:360:0.85);
\node at (12.5:1.9) {$b^{\circ}$};
\node at (50:1.6) {$(2b)^{\circ}$};
\node at (112.5:1.35) {$(3b)^{\circ}$};
\node at (255:1.4) {$210^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two straight lines intersect. A ray splits the upper angle into $32^{\circ}$ and $54^{\circ}$. Find its vertically opposite angle $x$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (47:2.5)--(227:2.5);
\draw (133:2.5)--(313:2.5);
\draw (0,0)--(79:2.5);
\draw (47:0.9) arc (47:79:0.9);
\draw (79:0.7) arc (79:133:0.7);
\draw (227:0.8) arc (227:313:0.8);
\node at (63:1.65) {$32^{\circ}$};
\node at (106:1.45) {$54^{\circ}$};
\node at (270:1.3) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
